PunBB 2.0.0
unreleased
====================

 * Fixed cross-site request forgery in post.php. FORUM_SKIP_CSRF_CONFIRM turned the global confirmation gate off for the whole script, and the token check that replaced it ran only for administrators and moderators, so any page a logged-in member visited could post in their name. Every 1.4 and 1.5 forum is affected. Backported for a 1.5.1 patch release.
 * get_remote_file() no longer fetches an https:// URL in cleartext. Where PHP has allow_url_fopen off, the socket fallback ignored the scheme and connected on port 80; the peer certificate is now verified and only http:// and https:// are fetchable at all, redirects included. Forums with allow_url_fopen off are affected - one caller is the extension hotfix manifest, whose hook code is eval()ed on every page load. The administration console now offers the update check when stream_socket_client() is available rather than fsockopen(), which the fetch no longer uses. Backported for a 1.5.1 patch release.
 * The password reset form no longer reveals which addresses have accounts. It answered four different ways - no such address, this one is the administrator's, this one asked recently, mail sent - all readable without an account. It now answers the same whatever the address turns out to be. An administrator's password was never resettable by mail; the form no longer says so either, so recover an administrator account through the database. Language packs must follow: 'No e-mail match', 'Email important' and 'Email flood' are gone from lang/*/login.php and 'Forget mail' is reworded. Backported for a 1.5.1 patch release.
 * The login cookie's hash now covers the user id (forum_cookie_hash()). Two accounts that still carried a pre-1.5 unsalted hash of the same password produced byte-identical cookies, so editing the id in one's own cookie logged in as the other. Everyone is logged out once when this version is installed, because cookies issued by the old format no longer validate.
 * random_key() draws from random_bytes() and random_int() instead of mt_rand() and uniqid(). It produces the session id, the per-visit CSRF secret, the password salt and every mailed activation key, all of which were reproducible from a seeded Mersenne Twister.
 * A visit that started before the online.csrf_token column existed no longer issues guessable CSRF tokens. The upgrade adds the column with an empty default and the refresh path never wrote it, so the token was sha1() of the target URL alone. The secret is now filled in on the next request, and a request that still finds none mints and stores one, so the token it issues is reproducible on the next request without being guessable.
 * The mysqli and mysqli_innodb drivers set the connection charset with mysqli_set_charset() instead of a bare SET NAMES query. SET NAMES moved the charset the server decodes by while escape() kept escaping by the one the client connected with.
 * forum_config_add() and the extension installer escape their values before writing them. forum_config_add() is the documented helper extensions call to add a setting and wrote both arguments into the INSERT raw.
 * New forum_js_escape() for a value placed inside an inline <script>. forum_htmlencode() is the wrong escaper there - a script element is raw text, so its entities never decode and a backslash walks through untouched. The board title in the Oxygen style and in both templates, and the six PUNBB.env values in footer.php, now use it; a style or extension writing a PHP value into a script block must do the same.
 * Escaped output that was written raw: category names in the profile moderator checklist, forum names in search results, the reverse-DNS hostname of an IP lookup on moderate.php, and the ban IP lists in the administration console.
 * A mailed password-reset key now expires an hour after it was sent (FORUM_PASSWORD_RESET_TTL, the same window a second request is refused in), and keys are compared with hash_equals(). Nothing expired them before, so a reset mail left in an old mailbox still worked months later, and the loose comparison read a key like '0e123456' as a number.
 * install.php writes $cookie_secure = 1 when $base_url is https. It was hardcoded to 0 whatever the address said, and upgrades preserved it: an https forum installed with an earlier version must set it in config.php by hand, or the cookie carrying the password hash keeps being sent in the clear.
 * The PHP session id is regenerated at login and at logout, so nothing planted under a fixed id survives the privilege change.
 * The flash message store no longer instantiates classes when it unserialises its session value. An extension that put an object into a flash message must store a scalar or an array instead.
 * CSRF tokens are compared with csrf_token_matches(), which uses hash_equals(), at all 13 sites that compared them with !==. An extension comparing generate_form_token() output should use it too.
 * The four moderator quick actions on viewtopic.php and moderate.php, the ban removal link in admin/bans.php and the extension enable/disable links in admin/extensions.php bind their token to the acting user's id, as every other action token already did. Links built by an earlier version are rejected, and an extension that rebuilds one of these tokens must append $forum_user['id'] to the target.
 * rewrite.php accepts only a plain entry point in the forum root as the target of its require(), and fires re_page_not_found before the 404 it produces, as the unmatched-URI branch already did. A rewrite rule is data an extension can add through the re_rewrite_rules hook, and the URI it matched is urldecode()d first; a rule that routes anywhere else now produces a 404.
 * Every generated cache file starts with an in-file guard, so a request that reaches it directly gets nothing. cache_config.php holds o_smtp_pass and previously only cache/.htaccess kept it off the web. Empty the cache/ directory when upgrading so the files are regenerated with the guard.
 * cache/.htaccess and img/avatars/.htaccess deny access the Apache 2.4 way, with the 2.2 form kept behind an IfModule. On 2.4 without mod_access_compat the old Order allow,deny was a configuration error - a 500 for the directory, not a denial. A server that ignores .htaccess needs its own rule denying cache/.
 * forum_mail() and smtp_mail() put only validated addresses in the envelope. The mailing list setting is typed by hand and nothing checked it, so each comma-separated part became a RCPT TO of its own; invalid parts are now dropped. is_valid_email() no longer accepts control characters, commas, semicolons or angle brackets inside a quoted local part, and no longer accepts a trailing newline.
 * A failed mail no longer prints the relay host, the port or the SMTP server's raw response on the error page. The page reached an unauthenticated visitor; the details are shown only when FORUM_DEBUG is set, and are encoded.
 * The login form verifies against a fixed dummy hash when the username matches no row, so an unknown username costs the same as a wrong password. It answered with the same message either way but not in the same time.
 * New hooks: fn_forum_session_regenerate_start, fn_forum_cookie_hash_start, fn_csrf_token_matches_start, fn_forum_store_csrf_token_qr_store_token and em_fn_forum_mail_recipients_start.
 * Added SECURITY.md, which describes how to report a vulnerability in this fork and what is out of scope. Three things it names are worth repeating here: admin/db_update.php still has no permission check, so delete it once an upgrade is finished; FORUM_SHOW_QUERIES prints every statement to whoever made the request, guest included, so do not set it on a public forum; and neither the login form nor the password reset form is rate limited.


PunBB 1.5.0
2026-08-29
====================

 * PHP 8.4 is now the minimum supported version; PHP 5 and 7 support is dropped.
 * Passwords are hashed with password_hash() from now on. Nothing stored before is rewritten in place: forum_password_verify() still reads the salted SHA-1 of 1.4, the unsalted SHA-1 of 1.3 and the MD5 of 1.2, and a row is upgraded only when its owner next signs in with the right password. The users.password column grew to VARCHAR(255) for it, which is database revision 6 - run admin/db_update.php.
 * Includes the upstream 1.4.5 and 1.4.6 releases: the PHP-compatibility groundwork of 1.4.5 and the 1.4.6 hardening of the email BBCode tag, where no tag may nest inside [email] and the email patterns run before the formatting ones.
 * Restored the fixes this fork had made on top of 1.4.4 that the upstream archives, built from plain 1.4.4, had reverted: pagination in userlist/admin, InnoDB detection on current MySQL, f.forum_desc in viewforum, the po_main_output_end hook, ident(40) for IPv6 addresses, the InnoDB transaction commit on close, the redeclaration guard in forum_remove_bad_characters() and the extension manifest's PHP version and extension checks.
 * Dependencies are managed by Composer 2: 'composer install --no-dev' must be run in the forum directory before the first request, because include/autoload.php requires vendor/autoload.php and stops the forum without it. The forum itself has no runtime packages - the autoloader is the only thing generated. .htaccess.dist denies access to vendor/ and the tooling manifests; merge it into your .htaccess.
 * Removed the 'mysql', 'mysql_innodb' and 'sqlite' (SQLite2) database drivers along with the PHP extensions they needed. Supported drivers are 'mysqli', 'mysqli_innodb', 'pgsql' and 'sqlite3'; a forum on a removed driver must change $db_type in config.php before db_update.php will run.
 * Replaced create_function() with closures in the BBCode parser and the admin index. Extensions hooking ps_do_bbcode_replace may push either callables or the old code strings into $replace/$replace_callback; the strings are compiled with the original semantics.
 * install.php and db_update.php now refuse to run unless PHP 8.4+, the mbstring, intl, json and xml extensions and at least one supported database extension are present.
 * Removed magic quotes handling.
 * Fixed the pgsql driver for the PgSql\Connection and PgSql\Result objects ext/pgsql returns since PHP 8.1.
 * Database drivers now own their failures: each sets its own error mode, catches the driver exception and renders the forum error page. $forum_db->query() no longer returns false on a failed query, and extensions relying on that return value must handle the error page instead.
 * Fixed the values passed to internal functions where a missing request key or a nullable column produced null. Absent inputs are normalised at the source; a request that cannot be honoured is now rejected instead of rendered off a missing row.
 * Declared all class properties explicitly and dropped the PHP 4 var declarations, so no class relies on dynamic properties.
 * Removed the @/**/ error-suppression idiom and handled the errors it hid, notably in the avatar upload path (getimagesize() failures now report a bad type instead of unpacking false).
 * Replaced utf8_decode()/utf8_encode(), xml_parser_free() and $http_response_header, all deprecated. Transliteration for URL and search slugs now goes through mbstring.
 * result() returns false for an empty result set on every driver.
 * MySQL 8 made GROUPS and RANK reserved words. The mysqli drivers now quote every generated identifier and table reference; $forum_db->quote_identifier() is available on all four drivers for extensions writing raw SQL.
 * The PHP session cookie now follows $cookie_path, $cookie_domain and $cookie_secure from config.php and is HttpOnly. Existing sessions are dropped on upgrade.
 * Removed forum_unregister_globals(); register_globals has not existed since PHP 5.4.
 * preparse_list_tag() no longer defaults $type: an optional parameter before a by-reference one is illegal in PHP 8.
 * Replaced the bundled phputf8 library with include/utf8.php, a shim over mbstring and PCRE. The 28 utf8_* names the forum and its extension API use keep their signatures and return values, but 16 phputf8 helpers no caller used are gone: utf8_str_split, utf8_str_pad, utf8_strcasecmp, utf8_strcspn, utf8_accents_to_ascii, utf8_is_ascii_ctrl, utf8_strip_ascii_ctrl, utf8_is_word_chars, utf8_is_valid, utf8_compliant, utf8_byte_position, utf8_bad_find, utf8_bad_findall, utf8_bad_replace, utf8_bad_strip and utf8_bad_explain. An extension calling one of them must switch to mbstring. mbstring is now required and mb_internal_encoding() is set to UTF-8 at bootstrap; an extension shipping its own copy of phputf8 must drop it.
 * Replaced the bundled idna_convert library with ext-intl, which is now required. IDN conversion follows UTS-46 instead of IDNA2003 and touches the host only: 'ss' is no longer substituted for 'ß', final sigma and ZWNJ/ZWJ survive, the host is case-folded, and a label with a leading/trailing hyphen or over 63 octets is passed through unconverted instead of being encoded. Paths, query strings, user info and email local parts are left alone.
 * get_current_url() now builds the scheme, host and port from $base_url in config.php instead of the request headers, so a proxy rewriting Host can no longer forge self-referential URLs or break the CSRF tokens keyed on them. $base_url must name the forum's public address; a $base_url with no host makes self-referential URLs root-relative.
 * Removed the bundled LABjs script loader. The Loader now emits plain <script> tags for every group, which is what LABjs emulated; ordering comes from the tag order and the native async/defer attributes. The ld_fn_render_js_labjs_start and ld_fn_render_js_labjs_end hooks are gone — an extension bound to them must move to ld_fn_render_js_simple_start / ld_fn_render_js_simple_end — and FORUM_DISABLE_ASYNC_JS_LOADER in config.php no longer does anything.
 * Dropped the asset build: the Ant script, YUI Compressor and the four bundled JARs are gone and nothing replaced them. The forum now serves include/js/*.js and style/Oxygen/Oxygen.css directly, so no Java and no Node are needed to install or develop it. Oxygen.min.css had never been minified — it was the hand-maintained stylesheet and is now named Oxygen.css.
 * update_search_index() no longer passes a null subject to the UTF-8 helpers: a reply has no subject, so every reply and every edit emitted a deprecation.
 * strip_search_index() returns early for an empty post list instead of building an invalid 'IN ()' query. Deleting a forum holding only topic redirects ended on the error page.
 * admin/reindex.php used the 'case X;' form, deprecated in PHP 8.5 and a candidate for removal in 9.0. The compile-time notice reached the browser and turned the rest of the page into 'headers already sent' warnings.
 * Removed stylesheets nothing loads: Oxygen.css, Oxygen_cs.css and Oxygen_ie6/7/8.css stopped being build inputs or served files in 2011-2015 and no longer describe the shipped Oxygen.min.css, and style/print.css was never referenced at all.


